place Zone_Atmosphere autumnsky at -80 -45 y=10
place Zone_Atmosphere autumnturned at -85 0 y=10
place Zone_Atmosphere autumnturned at -80 -45 y=10

# --- The sea round the ring: dolphins in the lagoon, a sunk crate in the north-east channel ------------------------------
place Creature_Dolphin dolphins at 20 -10 h=-3
place Loot_SunkenBarrel channelcrate at 60 70 h=-3 drop

# --- Raft's finds in the shallows round the ring and in the lagoon (lib_sea) ------------------------------------------------
call shallows r=139 deep=5 n=2

# ===== Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest (24 steps, 6 chapters) =============================================
info title=Four Seasons
info author=Custom Islands
info description=An atoll whose four islets each stand in a different season - snow, blossom, high summer, harvest - stuck since the weather-keeper's wheel stopped. Each season keeps a token behind its own kind of task. Lay all four in the year's wheel and the seasons turn again.
island on.arrive=message||A ring of islands round a lagoon - and it is snowing on the northern one, the eastern one is pink with blossom, the southern one shimmers in summer heat, and the western one is all gold and falling leaves.

story token|Season token|Placeable_Utopia_LightBottleWhite|A token of one season - a snowflake of glass, a blossom of silk, a sunburst of brass, a sheaf of gold wire.
story yearseed|Seed of the year|Seed_Birch|A seed that fell out of the year's wheel when it turned: it will grow in any season.

note almanac Maren's almanac | THE ALMANAC OF THE WEATHER-HOUSE\n\nFor sixty years I turned the year's wheel on every quarter-day, and the islets took their seasons in turn.\n\nIf you are reading this, I have stopped turning it, and each islet is stuck in its own season. The wheel will turn again for whoever lays the four tokens in it:\nWINTER's, at the top of the ice spire - the frost bear sleeps at its foot.\nSPRING's, with the shepherdess - she lost her lambs.\nSUMMER's, under the sunken bell on the reef.\nAUTUMN's, for whoever rings the harvest bells in the order of the rhyme.\n\nMy locker has what you'll need for the lambs.\n- Maren
note keeperlocker Weather-keeper's locker | Maren's locker: oilskins, a barometer - and a net launcher with its canisters, labelled FOR THE LAMBS.
loot keeperlocker NetGun*1;NetCanister*6;Rope*2
prop keeperlocker loot.refill=0
note frostverse The frost shrine's verse | (cut into the shrine's stone)\n\nAt the top of the ice the winter sleeps;\nat the foot of the ice the white bear keeps.\nClimb past the one to wake the other.
note wintertoken Winter's token | At the top of the ice spire, in a box of ice: a snowflake of glass that never melts.
loot wintertoken story:token*1;Wool*2
prop wintertoken loot.refill=0
note shepherdnote The shepherdess's note | (pinned to the pen's open gate)\n\nMy three lambs broke out when the blossom came and won't come home. Net them and they'll trot back to the pen.\nThe spring's token is in my box on the step - it's yours when they're home.\n- Liv
note springtoken Spring's token | The shepherdess's box: a blossom of silk that smells of spring - and cheese.
loot springtoken story:token*1;Cooked_GenericMeat*2
prop springtoken loot.refill=0
prop springtoken if.open=quest|11
prop springtoken else.open=message||Liv's box. Her note: it's yours when the lambs are home.
note diverlog The diver's log | SUMMER REEF - DIVER'S LOG\n\nThe summer bell sank in a squall; it's on the reef, eight metres, on a stone. The token is in a box under it.\nAir under the coral overhangs - two of them, between here and the bell.\nTurtles everywhere. They don't mind company.
note summertoken Summer's token | Under the sunken bell: a box with a sunburst of brass in it, warm even down here.
loot summertoken story:token*1;CopperOre*1
prop summertoken loot.refill=0
note rhyme The harvest rhyme | (painted on the barn door)\n\nFirst we plough, then we sow,\nthen we reap the golden row,\nlast we store it, safe and sound -\nring the year the right way round.
note autumntoken Autumn's token | In the barn, where the bells' ringing shook it loose from the rafters: a sheaf of gold wire.
loot autumntoken story:token*1;Seed_Pine*2
prop autumntoken loot.refill=0
prop autumntoken obj.name=autumntoken
prop autumntoken beh.hidden=1
note lastpage Maren's last page | (it fell out of the wheel's hub as it turned)\n\nYou did it. The north is thawing, the east is ripening, the south is turning gold and the west has its first frost. Next quarter-day, turn it again - or don't. The islets will take their seasons as they come.\n\nMy chest is yours. Plant something.\n- Maren
note keeperchest Weather-keeper's chest | Maren's chest: the plans for her planting beds - small and medium - seeds of every season, a coat for winter and a hat for summer.
loot keeperchest Blueprint_Cropplot_Small_Tier3*1;Blueprint_Cropplot_Medium_Tier3*1;Seed_Strawberry*4;Seed_Watermelon*4;Seed_Mango*3;Seed_Birch*3;Equipment_LeatherChest*1;Hat_Fishing*1
prop keeperchest loot.refill=0
prop keeperchest if.open=signal|turned
prop keeperchest else.open=message||Maren's chest. A tag on it: WHEN THE WHEEL TURNS.
note diverbox Diver's box | A box under the diver's hut: a mask, fins, dried fish.
loot diverbox Cooked_Herring*2;Rope*2;Plastic*2
prop diverbox loot.refill=0
note channelcrate Sunk crate | A crate in a channel between the islets: the keeper's supplies that never arrived.
loot channelcrate MetalOre*2;Scrap*3;Nail*6
prop channelcrate loot.refill=0
note winterbox Winter landing box | A box at the winter landing: blankets and a flask.
loot winterbox Wool*2;PlasticBottle_Water*2
prop winterbox loot.refill=0

prop bellplough obj.name=bellplough
prop bellplough beh.use=Ring the PLOUGH bell
prop bellplough on.use=message||PLOUGH - a deep, dull clang.\nsignal||b1\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/bicyclebell
prop bellsow obj.name=bellsow
prop bellsow beh.use=Ring the SOW bell
prop bellsow if.use=signal|b1
prop bellsow on.use=message||SOW - a lighter note.\nsignal||b2\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/bicyclebell
prop bellsow else.use=message||A sour note - the leaves shiver off the trees. "Ring the year the right way round."
prop bellreap obj.name=bellreap
prop bellreap beh.use=Ring the REAP bell
prop bellreap if.use=signal|b2
prop bellreap on.use=message||REAP - bright as a sickle.\nsignal||b3\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/bicyclebell
prop bellreap else.use=message||A sour note - the leaves shiver off the trees. "Ring the year the right way round."
prop bellstore obj.name=bellstore
prop bellstore beh.use=Ring the STORE bell
prop bellstore if.use=signal|b3\n!signal|rung
prop bellstore on.use=message||STORE - and the four notes run together into a chord. In the barn, something falls from the rafters with a soft chink.\nsignal||rung\nshow|autumntoken\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/bicyclebell
prop bellstore else.use=message||A sour note - the leaves shiver off the trees. "Ring the year the right way round."
prop wheel obj.name=wheel
prop wheel beh.use=Lay the four season tokens in the year's wheel
prop wheel if.use=quest|21\ntake|story:token|4
prop wheel on.use=message||Snowflake, blossom, sunburst, sheaf - each into its socket on the rim. The wheel shudders and begins to turn. Out across the lagoon the seasons slide round: the north islet's snow turns to mist and thaw, the east's blossom to summer green, the south's heat to autumn gold, the west's falling leaves to the first frost. A page drops out of the wheel's hub, and a seed.\nsignal||turned\nhide|wheel\nshow|wheelturning\nhide|wintersky\nshow|winterturned\nhide|springsky\nshow|springturned\nhide|summersky\nshow|summerturned\nhide|autumnsky\nshow|autumnturned\nshow|lastpage\ngive||story:yearseed*1\nsound||event:/exploring/utopia/waterwheel_rotate
prop wheel else.use=message||The year's wheel, stopped, four empty sockets on its rim. Maren's almanac says what goes in them.
